I’m afraid there isn’t a 3‑star hotel in the moderate range that lists free Wi‑Fi in our database. If you’re willing to be a little flexible, we could look at:

* a 3‑star place that’s a bit cheaper – they usually still have decent internet;
* a 2‑star hotel that’s moderate‑priced and offers free Wi‑Fi;
* or simply head straight to the town centre on Wednesday, pop into a few hotels and ask if they have any rooms left. Many smaller hotels will let you check in on the spot without a prior reservation, and you can sort out the Wi‑Fi later – it’s a bit of a gamble, but it can save you the hassle of booking ahead.

Let me know which option sounds best, and I’ll lock in the details for you.
